ph (b)(2)\"],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:9de5ee054c2e86c95eab34e3fb5caf4a2574c7a7fb3d5c216173a839c2575cc2\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"(1) Subject to the exceptions provided in paragraph (b)(2) of this section, employment periods prior to a break in service of seven years or more need not be counted in determining whether the employee has been employed by the employer for at least 12 months.\"],\"scope_text\":\"Applies in determining whether an employee has been employed by the employer for at least 12 months when there is a break in service of seven years or more, subject to the exceptions provided in paragraph (b)(2) of this section.\",\"section_id\":\"section-1\",\"start\":704,\"summary\":\"Subject to the exceptions in paragraph (b)(2) of this section, employment periods prior to a break in service of seven years or more need not be counted in determining whether the employee has been employed by the employer for at least 12 months.\",\"target_ids\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
      "dcterms:references": [
        {
          "@id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:26fe08f6354f5e8fca664152460c5bb5bbf2177b6f0ca7e7e0d40541a6f61f7a"
        },
        {
